# CODEOWNERS example for a Tx Studio repository. Copy to .github/CODEOWNERS (GitHub also looks
# in the repository root and docs/, in that order, and uses the first one it finds).
#
# How it works (GitHub docs, about-code-owners):
# - Code owners are asked to review every pull request that touches their files. With the main
#   ruleset's "Require review from Code Owners", their approval is needed to merge.
# - Owners must have write access. A team must be visible (not secret) and have explicit write
#   access to the repository, even if its members already have access another way.
# - The LAST matching pattern wins, so put the general rule first and the specific ones after.
# - Several owners for one pattern go on the same line; any one of them can approve.
# - Patterns are case-sensitive on GitHub, even though macOS and Windows disks are not.
# - Unlike .gitignore: no "!" negation, no [a-z] ranges, no "\#" escapes.
# - A line with a syntax error, or an owner that does not exist, is skipped (GitHub shows the
#   error when you open the file on github.com).
#
# Teams used below (create them under the organization, both visible):
#   @YOUR-ORG/addon-devs        everyone who writes addon code (write access)
#   @YOUR-ORG/release-managers  two or more people who may tag releases (maintain access)

# Default owner for everything.
*                       @YOUR-ORG/addon-devs

# Files that decide what ships to players, where it is uploaded and who can do it.
# GitHub recommends code owners on .github/workflows so workflow changes need approval.
/.github/               @YOUR-ORG/release-managers
/.pkgmeta               @YOUR-ORG/release-managers
/*.toc                  @YOUR-ORG/release-managers
/LICENSE                @YOUR-ORG/release-managers

# Saved-variable migrations can destroy players' settings: two pairs of eyes.
# (Adjust the path to where your addon keeps its database code.)
/Database.lua           @YOUR-ORG/addon-devs @YOUR-ORG/release-managers

# Translations: translators may review each other's locale files.
# /Locales/deDE.lua     @translator-github-name
